| Contracts awarded, {{dfma_evidence.json:demand_latest_year}} (current prices) | S${{dfma_evidence.json:contracts_awarded_latest_sgd_m|,.0f}} million, {{dfma_evidence.json:contracts_awarded_growth_2019_latest_pct|.0f}}% above 2019 | `results/dfma_evidence.json` |
| Building work share of contracts awarded / progress payments, {{dfma_evidence.json:demand_latest_year}} | {{dfma_evidence.json:building_share_of_contracts_latest_pct|.1f}}% / {{dfma_evidence.json:building_share_of_payments_latest_pct|.1f}}% | `results/dfma_evidence.json` |
| Construction, marine and process work permit holders, Dec {{dfma_evidence.json:cmp_latest_year}} | {{dfma_evidence.json:cmp_latest|,.0f}} (2019 to 2020: {{dfma_evidence.json:cmp_2019_to_2020_pct|.1f}}%) | `results/dfma_evidence.json` |

The adoption figures are four single figures from BCA releases (2019, a September 2022 "today" figure, 2023,
2024); the bases differ (the 2019 figure does not say "by GFA"). With four points a correlation of any sign
is uninformative, and the observed one is not significant. The open data cannot separate a DfMA effect from
the pandemic, foreign-worker supply and the demand boom shown above. A further reason it cannot: factory work
for precast and PPVC is counted in manufacturing, or abroad, not in Singapore construction value added, so a
shift off-site changes who is counted in the denominator as well as how efficient the work is.

### 3. Illustrative model: one hypothetical block, four methods

All parameters are in `params/model.json`. Every one is a labelled assumption with a low and a high bound
(the high bound of `prefab_mep_time_cut` equals BCA's published "up to" figure for prefab MEP); none is calibrated to a project. BCA's
published figures are used only as checks on the output. Off-site factory labour is outside the model, so
"site productivity" is GFA per site man-day. Base case: {{model_base.json:scenarios.conventional.gfa_m2|,.0f}} m2 GFA.

| Method | Site man-days | Duration, days | Site m2 per man-day | Manpower saving | Duration saving, days | Takt, days per floor |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Conventional | {{model_base.json:scenarios.conventional.site_man_days|,.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.conventional.duration_days|.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.conventional.site_productivity_m2_per_md|.2f}} | - | - | {{model_base.json:scenarios.conventional.takt_days|.1f}} |
| Precast frame | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast.site_man_days|,.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast.duration_days|.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast.site_productivity_m2_per_md|.2f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast.manpower_saving_pct|.1f}}% | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast.duration_saving_days|.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast.takt_days|.1f}} |
| Precast + prefab MEP | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast_prefab_mep.site_man_days|,.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast_prefab_mep.duration_days|.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast_prefab_mep.site_productivity_m2_per_md|.2f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast_prefab_mep.manpower_saving_pct|.1f}}% | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast_prefab_mep.duration_saving_days|.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.precast_prefab_mep.takt_days|.1f}} |
| PPVC | {{model_base.json:scenarios.ppvc.site_man_days|,.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.ppvc.duration_days|.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.ppvc.site_productivity_m2_per_md|.2f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.ppvc.manpower_saving_pct|.1f}}% | {{model_base.json:scenarios.ppvc.duration_saving_days|.0f}} | {{model_base.json:scenarios.ppvc.takt_days|.1f}} |

